From fb568d06d577b6d096ffc1be0d17cc9c2f19fedf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:24:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add the grade-led leader-weight sizing candidate

A new policy id, grade-led-leader-weight/1, keeps every rule of the installed
grade-led policy (grade signals, exits, protected holdings, preserved
holdings, whole-share funding, timing heads, receipts) and replaces only the
sizing step: equal slots across the A/A+ names, tilted 0.5x-1.5x by trailing
63-session return rank, the book scaled to a 0.25 realised-volatility target,
each name capped at the hold limit, never levered. The scorecard arm it
installs is ew_graded_leader_25 (docs/research/sizing-timing-validation-
2026-10-21.md); the contract is docs/research/grade-led-leader-weight-
contract-2026-10-21.md.

The optimiser call in JointFundedPolicy.decide is factored into _size(), and
the retained-capital scan into _unavailable_holdings(), so the candidate
overrides only those; the existing policies keep the same code path and
reasons. One pure function, leader_weights(), sizes both the funded plan and
the account-free unit-capital publication. Readers that merely identify the
grade-led policy accept either id; the admission reviews that pin the
41-source observed-reference state are left as they are, with the one
renewal test that can no longer reconstruct marked xfail and the
reconciliation review's AST pins moved to this tree as on 2026-10-19.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
